Article 5 (Issuance of Certificates)
(1) A certificate issued by the Director General of the National Court Administration shall contain the following matters: <Amended on November 6, 2019>
1. Name of the subscribing agency, etc., receiving certification;
2. Administrative digital-signature verification key of the subscribing agency, etc.;
3. Administrative digital-signature method used by the Certification Management Center and the subscribing agency, etc.;
4. Serial number of the certificate;
5. Validity period of the certificate;
6. Indication of the Supreme Court as the certification authority;
7. Matters concerning any restrictions on the scope or purpose of use of the certificate.
(2) The validity period of a certificate shall be determined by the Certification Management Center in consideration of the scope of use and security of the technology employed.
(3) Where a certification authority issues a certificate, it shall use an administrative digital signature created with an administrative digital-signature generation key. <Newly Inserted on November 6, 2019>
